Subject: [PATCH] runtime: reclaim completed command buffers beyond the warm pool bound

Keep command pools alive, but rotate idle pools and free/trim excess completed
command buffers on the next encoding thread. A heavy frame must not retain
thousands of command-stream BOs for the process lifetime. All releases pass
through the exit guard and are primed before the runtime starts its workers.

